  "text": "Compared with a regular iPhone, a few things move around. There's no face ID. You unlock it with touch ID in the side button. The volume buttons sit on the top edge. The outer screen is shaped like a D, square by the hinge and rounded on the outside with its controls down the right edge. And the USB-C port sits low on the left half, out of the way when you use it like a laptop. Inside, it runs the same A20 Pro chip as the iPhone 18 Pro.",
